<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch unadjusted unemployment rises in Oct-Dec.</title>
<headline>Dutch unadjusted unemployment rises in Oct-Dec.</headline>
<dateline>VOORBURG, Netherlands 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch non-seasonally adjusted unemployment rose to an average of 432,000 in October-December from 431,000 in September-November, the Central Bureau of Statistics (CBS) said.  </p>
<p>DUTCH REGISTERED UNEMPLOYMENT NON-SEASONALLY ADJUSTED</p>
<p>			   Oct-Dec 96     Sept-Nov 96     Oct-Dec 95</p>
<p> total number	   432,000	  431,000	  459,000</p>
<p> pct of labour force    6.6		6.5		7.0</p>
<p>DUTCH REGISTERED UNEMPLOYMENT SEASONALLY ADJUSTED</p>
<p>			    Oct-Dec 96   Sept-Nov 96     Oct-Dec 95</p>
<p> total number	   432,000	  432,000	  458,000</p>
<p> pct of labour force    6.5		6.5		6.9</p>
<p>NOTES - Percentages are calculated as percentage of average 1995 labour force (6.596 million). By international standards, the CBS uses a narrow definition of unemployment. Figures are compiled from job centre registrations and CBS survey.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom, +31 20 504 5000</p>
</text>
